From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:33:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] soundwire: qcom: force runtime suspend across system
 sleep

The controller only has runtime PM ops, and a peripheral kept
runtime-active (the WCD9390 on the AYN Odin 3, held for jack detection)
keeps it active through s2idle, together with the LPASS macro clocks it
uses. Force the runtime suspend across system sleep, so jack detection
keeps working while awake but the ADSP can release LPASS in s2idle.
Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/4c945ec5b28176c8580059a1c5ab6176ac5f3104/packages/kernel/patches/0564-soundwire-qcom-force-runtime-suspend-across-system-sleep.patch

[mzak: picked from portare-ch/portareos devices/SM8550/patches/linux/1123 (= armada-os 0564) for
 the OnePlus Pad 4 (SM8850): the WCD9395's SoundWire controllers have the same runtime-only PM ops.
 Qualcomm kernel-topics PR #2177 carries the same idea for Glymur (cxsd / ddr / aosd stayed 0 in s2idle).]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 6812f4c09..84ed663a0 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1926,6 +1926,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops swrm_dev_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(swrm_runtime_suspend, swrm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
